VENV = Virtual environment
A self contained python bubble
Using its own python interpretor and own installed packages
Different projects use different versions of the same library

ONE VENV per project
Always activat before project start: ``` source .venv/bin/activate
No need to commit
New terminals need reactivation
'ModuleNotFoundError' = likely not in the right venv
Dependencies (deps) eg pygame, requests... need installing in venv and recording in dep file


PYGAME = Open source pygame library
Installed in ~/practice/my-work/games/asteroids2/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages$


GAME LOOPS
the most basic game loop has 3 stages:
1 - Check player input
2 - Update game world
3 - Game -> Screen

EVENT DRIVEN MODEL
Reacting to the actions
- moving, clicking the mouse
- pressing a key
- zooming, resizing, closing window
Pygame creates an EVENT object (KEYDOWN, MOUSEMOTION, QUIT etc)
Adds to an event queue, a 'to-do' list for all actions since last frame
---pygame.event.get()
- return list of EVENT objects
- empties the queue upon call
- now handled, will not appear in next frame
~~~EXAMPLE~~~
for event in pygame.event.get():
    events = pygame.event.get()
    print(events)
[<Event(1025-MouseButtonDown {'pos': (345, 200), 'button': 1})>,
 <Event(768-KeyDown {'key': 32, 'unicode': ' '})>]
# key: value
~~~       ~~~
for event in pygame.event.get():
    if event.type == pygame.QUIT:
        running = False

    elif event.type == pygame.KEYDOWN:
        print("A key was pressed:", event.key)

    elif event.type == pygame.MOUSEBUTTONDOWN:
        print("Mouse clicked at", event.pos)
